# Comprehensive Code Audit Report: Agent 10

**Target Files Audited:**
1. `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`
2. `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`
3. `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`
4. `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`
5. `new/client/src/pages/DashboardEnhanced.jsx`

---

## 1. `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`

### [UM-01] CRITICAL RUNTIME CRASH: Undefined Function Call `S.roleBadge`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 1589–1598
- **Category:** UI Rendering / TypeError
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  1588: {resetTarget.role && (
  1589:   <span
  1590:     style={S.roleBadge(
  1591:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).color,
  1592:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).bg,
  1593:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).border,
  1594:     )}
  1595:   >
  1596:     {getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).label}
  1597:   </span>
  1598: )}
  ```
- **Explanation:** In the styles object `S` (defined at line 84), there is no property named `roleBadge`. The badge helper function is named `regionPill` (`regionPill: (color, bg, border) => ({ ... })` at line 258, as used in lines 1090, 1100, 1111, 1122). Clicking the "Reset Password" button sets `resetTarget` and renders this modal, immediately crashing the app with `TypeError: S.roleBadge is not a function`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  {resetTarget.role && (
    <span
      style={S.regionPill(
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).color,
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).bg,
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).border,
      )}
    >
      {getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).label}
    </span>
  )}
  ```

---

### [UM-02] React Memory Leak: Uncleaned `setTimeout` & Unmounted Fetch
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Line 616
- **Category:** React State Management / Memory Leak
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  612: setIsModalOpen(false);
  613: // Delay background sync slightly so optimistic row renders first,
  614: // then merge — keeping the new user visible even if the server
  615: // response is still filtered (e.g. before a server restart).
  616: setTimeout(() => fetchData(true, true), 800);
  ```
- **Explanation:** If the user creates or edits a user and immediately navigates away from `/users` within 800ms, the timer fires and triggers `fetchData(true, true)` which calls `setUsers`, `setRegions`, etc. on an unmounted component.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  // Store timer in a ref to clean up on unmount:
  const syncTimerRef = useRef(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      if (syncTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(syncTimerRef.current);
    };
  }, []);

  // In handleSubmit:
  setIsModalOpen(false);
  if (syncTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(syncTimerRef.current);
  syncTimerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
    fetchData(true, true);
  }, 800);
  ```

---

### [UM-03] Missing Unmount Cancellation in Initial `fetchData`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 475–477
- **Category:** React State Management / Async Race Condition
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  475: useEffect(() => {
  476:   if (["it_admin", "it_manager", "it"].includes(user?.role)) fetchData();
  477: }, [user]);
  ```
- **Explanation:** `fetchData` has no active/mounted cancellation flag. If the user session updates or the component unmounts while API requests (`/users` or `/facilities/all-regions`) are pending, state updates are performed on an unmounted component.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    let isMounted = true;
    if (["it_admin", "it_manager", "it"].includes(user?.role)) {
      fetchData(false, false, () => isMounted);
    }
    return () => {
      isMounted = false;
    };
  }, [user]);
  ```

---

### [UM-04] Filter Leak: All Admins & IT Personnel Forced into Regional Filter Results
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 734–748
- **Category:** UI Rendering & Filter Logic
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  734: const filteredUsers = users.filter((u) => {
  735:   const byRegion =
  736:     !filterRegion ||
  737:     u.location === filterRegion ||
  738:     u.role === "admin" ||
  739:     u.role === "it_admin" ||
  740:     u.role === "it_manager" ||
  741:     u.role === "it";
  742:   const byRole = ...
  ```
- **Explanation:** When an administrator filters by a specific region (e.g., "Hassi Messaoud"), `byRegion` returns `true` for all users with roles `admin`, `it_admin`, `it_manager`, or `it`, regardless of whether their location matches the selected region or is blank. This completely breaks region filtering for auditing staff assigned to specific facilities.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const filteredUsers = users.filter((u) => {
    const byRegion =
      !filterRegion ||
      u.location === filterRegion ||
      (!u.location && ["admin", "it_admin", "it_manager", "superuser"].includes(u.role));
    const byRole =
      !filterRole ||
      u.role === filterRole ||
      (filterRole === "it_manager" && ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)) ||
      (filterRole === "it_admin" && ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role));
    return byRegion && byRole;
  });
  ```

---

### [UM-05] Missing `superuser` Accounting in Summary Tiles
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 728–732
- **Category:** Edge Case / Data Integrity
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  728: const totalUsers = users.length;
  729: const adminCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "admin").length;
  730: const itAdminCount = users.filter((u) => ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)).length;
  731: const itCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "it").length;
  732: const standardCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "user").length;
  ```
- **Explanation:** Accounts with `superuser` role (which exist in the DB and auth middleware) are omitted from all role counts, causing the sum of individual role counts to not match `totalUsers`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const totalUsers = users.length;
  const adminCount = users.filter((u) => ["admin", "superuser"].includes(u.role)).length;
  const itAdminCount = users.filter((u) => ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)).length;
  const itCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "it").length;
  const standardCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "user").length;
  ```

