## 3. `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`

### [ST-01] Fatal TypeError: Undefined Property Access on `facilityEdits[facId]`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`, Lines 287–293
- **Category:** UI Rendering / TypeError
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  286: try {
  287:   const data = facilityEdits[facId];
  288:   await api.put(`/facilities/${facId}`, {
  289:     operator_status: data.operator_status,
  290:     country: data.country,
  291:     ogmp_membership_year: Number(data.ogmp_membership_year),
  292:     reconciliation_threshold: Number(data.reconciliation_threshold),
  293:   });
  ```
- **Explanation:** If a user clicks the Save button for a facility before modifying any of its input fields, `facilityEdits[facId]` is `undefined`. Accessing `data.operator_status` immediately throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'operator_status')`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const fac = facilities.find(f => f.id === facId);
  const data = facilityEdits[facId] || fac || {};
  await api.put(`/facilities/${facId}`, {
    operator_status: data.operator_status || fac?.operator_status || "operated",
    country: data.country || fac?.country || "Algeria",
    ogmp_membership_year: Number(data.ogmp_membership_year || fac?.ogmp_membership_year || 2023),
    reconciliation_threshold: Number(data.reconciliation_threshold || fac?.reconciliation_threshold || 20.0),
  });
  ```

---

### [ST-02] Unmounted Memory Leak Across 12 State Setters in `loadSettings`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`, Lines 130–180
- **Category:** React State Management / Memory Leak
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  const loadSettings = async () => {
    ...
    setGwpStandard(data.gwp_standard || "AR5");
    setGwpHorizon(data.gwp_horizon || "100");
    setReconciliationThreshold(data.reconciliation_threshold || 20);
    setCopernicusUsername(copernicus.username || "");
    ...
    setLoading(false);
  };
  useEffect(() => { loadSettings(); }, []);
  ```
- **Explanation:** If the user leaves the Settings tab while `api.get("/settings")` or `api.get("/facilities")` is in flight, all 12 state setters are called on an unmounted component.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    let isMounted = true;
    const loadSettings = async () => {
      try {
        const [settingsRes, facRes] = await Promise.all([
          api.get("/settings"),
          api.get("/facilities"),
        ]);
        if (!isMounted) return;
        // Proceed with state setters...
      } catch (err) {
        if (!isMounted) return;
        console.error("Failed to load settings:", err);
      } finally {
        if (isMounted) setLoading(false);
      }
    };
    loadSettings();
    return () => { isMounted = false; };
  }, []);
  ```

---

### [ST-03] UI Formatting Artifact: Copernicus QA Slider Displays IEEE 754 Float Artifacts
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`, Lines 1134–1147
- **Category:** UI Rendering / Precision Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  1134: <span className="slider-val">
  1135:   &ge; {copernicusQaThreshold}
  1136: </span>
  ...
  1139: <input
  1140:   type="range"
  1141:   min="0.3"
  1142:   max="0.9"
  1143:   step="0.05"
  1144:   value={copernicusQaThreshold}
  1145:   onChange={(e) => setCopernicusQaThreshold(Number(e.target.value))}
  1146: />
  ```
- **Explanation:** Stepping by `0.05` on an input range results in values such as `0.5500000000000002` due to IEEE 754 precision. Rendering `{copernicusQaThreshold}` directly displays `≥ 0.5500000000000002` in the UI.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  <span className="slider-val">
    &ge; {Number(copernicusQaThreshold).toFixed(2)}
  </span>
  ```

