## 4. `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`

### [CI-01] Async Race Condition: Operational Defaults Overwritten by Global Defaults
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`, Lines 108–130
- **Category:** React State Management / Async Race Condition
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  108: const opDefaults = getUserOperationalDefaults(user, facilitiesData);
  109: if (opDefaults.isRestricted || facilitiesData.length === 1) {
  110:   if (opDefaults.defaultActivity) setCurrentActivity(opDefaults.defaultActivity);
  111:   if (opDefaults.defaultDivision) setCurrentDivision(opDefaults.defaultDivision);
  112:   if (opDefaults.defaultFacilityId) setCurrentRegion(opDefaults.defaultFacilityId);
  113: }
  ...
  122: useEffect(() => {
  123:   loadIntensityData();
  124: }, [currentActivity, currentDivision, currentRegion, selectedYear, currentSegment]);
  ```
- **Explanation:** On initial mount, `currentActivity`, `currentDivision`, and `currentRegion` default to `"all"`. Line 122 immediately launches `loadIntensityData()` querying global enterprise data. Simultaneously, `init()` runs. When `init()` finishes, it updates state with restricted defaults, triggering a second fetch. If the first fetch resolves after the second, the restricted view is overwritten with global enterprise data, leaking cross-facility metrics.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const [isReady, setIsReady] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    let isMounted = true;
    const init = async () => {
      try {
        const [facRes, settingsRes, filterRes] = await Promise.all([
          api.get("/facilities"),
          api.get("/settings"),
          api.get("/filters/available"),
        ]);
        if (!isMounted) return;
        const facs = Array.isArray(facRes.data) ? facRes.data : facRes.data?.data || [];
        setFacilities(facs);
        const opDefaults = getUserOperationalDefaults(user, facs);
        if (opDefaults.isRestricted || facs.length === 1) {
          if (opDefaults.defaultActivity) setCurrentActivity(opDefaults.defaultActivity);
          if (opDefaults.defaultDivision) setCurrentDivision(opDefaults.defaultDivision);
          if (opDefaults.defaultFacilityId) setCurrentRegion(opDefaults.defaultFacilityId);
        }
        setIsReady(true);
      } catch (err) {
        if (isMounted) console.error("Init failed:", err);
      }
    };
    init();
    return () => { isMounted = false; };
  }, [user]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isReady) return;
    loadIntensityData();
  }, [isReady, currentActivity, currentDivision, currentRegion, selectedYear, currentSegment]);
  ```

---

### [CI-02] Heatmap Type Mismatch & Undefined Data Crash
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`, Lines 424–428 & 939–942
- **Category:** UI Rendering / TypeError & Strict Equality Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  424: let yearData = item.data;
  425: if (currentRegion !== "all") {
  426:   yearData = yearData.filter(
  427:     (d) => d.facility_id.toString() === currentRegion,
  428:   );
  429: }
  ...
  939: {rawTrendData.map((yData) => {
  940:   const record = yData.data.find(
  941:     (r) => r.facility_id === facData.facility_id,
  942:   );
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  1. If `item.data` or `yData.data` is `null`/`undefined`, `.filter()` and `.find()` throw `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`.
  2. `r.facility_id === facData.facility_id` fails if one is a `string` (e.g. `"1"`) and the other a `number` (`1`), causing every cell in the Heatmap table to render as `"-"`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  let yearData = Array.isArray(item.data) ? item.data : [];
  if (currentRegion !== "all") {
    yearData = yearData.filter(
      (d) => String(d.facility_id) === String(currentRegion),
    );
  }
  // In Heatmap JSX:
  const record = Array.isArray(yData.data)
    ? yData.data.find((r) => String(r.facility_id) === String(facData.facility_id))
    : null;
  ```

---

### [CI-03] Potential Crash in Heatmap Tooltip on Null Intensity
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`, Line 954
- **Category:** UI Rendering / TypeError
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  954: title={`${yData.year} Intensity: ${val.toFixed(3)} kg CO2e/BOE`}
  ```
- **Explanation:** If `val` is `null`, `undefined`, or `NaN`, `val.toFixed(3)` throws `TypeError: val.toFixed is not a function`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  title={`${yData.year} Intensity: ${typeof val === 'number' && !isNaN(val) ? val.toFixed(3) : '-'} kg CO2e/BOE`}
  ```

